course: dictionary
lesson: 12617
title: Disinclined: not wanting to
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Disinclined means not wanting to do something. It is a more formal word than "don't want to", and you will meet it in books and stories. «Mia felt disinclined to go out in the rain.» Mia did not want to go out, and the rain was the reason.
explain: Look at the words around it. In «disinclined to help», the word "to" shows that an action comes next. Try your meaning in the sentence: swap in "unwilling" or "didn't feel like it". If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Disinclined can also mean not in the mood, often because you are tired or lazy. «After the long match, Sam was disinclined to tidy his room.» Sam is not refusing for a big reason. He feels too tired to bother.
fact: Disinclined means not wanting to do something; unwilling.
fact: Disinclined is an adjective, so it describes a person: «She was disinclined to help.»
fact: Disinclined is often used in formal writing. In everyday talk, people say «I don't feel like it» instead.
fact: Common phrases are «disinclined to help» and «feel disinclined to».
fact: When you are disinclined, you are not in the mood, often because you are tired or lazy.
exercise: «The dog was disinclined to leave its warm bed.» What does disinclined mean here? | Happy to run far away | Fast and ready | Very excited to | *Not wanting to, unwilling
exercise: Which everyday phrase means the same as «disinclined to help»? | I will help you later | I can help you now | *I don't feel like helping | I am glad to help
exercise: «Tired after the match, Sam was disinclined to tidy his room.» Why might Sam be disinclined? | Because his room is already clean | *Because he is tired and feels lazy | Because he loves tidying | Because he was too excited to sleep
test: «The children were disinclined to walk home in the snow.» What does disinclined mean? | Very cold and wet | Eager to hurry | Lost in the snow | *Unwilling to do it
test: Which word best completes this sentence? «Dad felt ___ to cook after a long day at work.» | Eager | Ready | Thrilled | *Disinclined
exam: «My brother was disinclined to share his sweets.» What does disinclined mean in this sentence? | Very hungry | Happy to give them away | *Unwilling to share | Eager to share
